<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Junín Region</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Junín Department</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Junín is a region of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>, stretching from the Andean highlands around Lake Junín to the Amazonian forests of the east; its capital is <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huancayo">Huancayo</a>. Its high plateau was the scene of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-junin">Battle of Junín</a> in August 1824, a cavalry victory of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simon-bolivar">Simón Bolívar</a>'s forces over the royalists, after which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> was named. Its economy rests on mining, farming and the trade of the Mantaro valley.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/junin-region.jpg" alt="Junín Region" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gu7y2004 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Monta%C3%B1as_en_la_sierra_de_Jun%C3%ADn,_Per%C3%BA.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
